@startuml linear-implementer
title "LinearImplementer — ticket delegated to Jardinero"

scale 0.8
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam ArrowColor Black
skinparam StateBorderColor Black
skinparam StateFontColor Black
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor White
skinparam NoteBorderColor Black
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BackgroundColor<<Package>> LightBlue
    BackgroundColor<<Final>> LightGreen
    BackgroundColor<<Error>> LightCoral
}

state "OWNED — the PR is a draft, PrMaintainer stays out" as owned <<Package>> {

    state "li_pending" as Pending
        Pending: - instance exists, no run dispatched
        Pending: - recovery finds these and dispatches

    state "li_implementing" as Implementing
        Implementing: - LinearImplementer running
        Implementing: - iteration, branch
        Implementing: - dispatched again if no run is alive

    state "li_verifying" as Verifying
        Verifying: - LinearVerifier running
        Verifying: - verified_sha, transient_retries
        Verifying: - dispatched again if no run is alive

    state "li_needs_human" as NeedsHuman <<Error>>
        NeedsHuman: - OPEN, not final: can be advanced
        NeedsHuman: - reason, verifier issues

    state "li_dismissed" as Dismissed <<Final>>
        Dismissed: - a person stopped it instead of retrying
}

state "RELEASED — PrMaintainer maintains the PR" as released <<Package>> {

    state "li_waiting_pr" as WaitingPr
        WaitingPr: - PR ready for review
        WaitingPr: - checked hourly until merged or closed

    state "li_done" as Done <<Final>>
        Done: - PR merged; Linear closes the ticket

    state "li_abandoned" as Abandoned <<Final>>
        Abandoned: - PR closed without merging
}

[*] -r-> Pending: OnIssueAssigned

Pending -r-> Implementing: handleStateLiPending\nOnPeriodicCheck(dispatch owed)\nOnSystemRecovery(dispatch owed)
Implementing --r-> Verifying: OnSandboxRunSucceeded(draft PR opened)

Implementing -d-> Implementing: OnSandboxRunFailed\nOnPeriodicCheck(run lost)\nOnSystemRecovery(run lost)\n\n\n\n\n\n
Implementing -u[#Red]-> NeedsHuman: handleStateLiImplementing(no iterations left)\nOnSandboxRunSucceeded(no PR)

NeedsHuman -d-> Implementing: OnOperatorRetry\nOnIssueAssigned\nOnIssueCommented\nOnPrComment
NeedsHuman -r-> Dismissed: OnOperatorDismiss

Verifying -l-> Implementing: OnSandboxRunSucceeded(reject, iterations left)
Verifying -u-> Verifying: OnSandboxRunSucceeded(no verdict)\nOnSandboxRunFailed\nOnPeriodicCheck(run lost)\nOnSystemRecovery(run lost)
Verifying -u[#Red]-> NeedsHuman: handleStateLiVerifying(no iterations left)\nOnSandboxRunSucceeded(accept, release failed)\nOnPeriodicCheck(outcome lost)

Verifying --d-> WaitingPr: OnSandboxRunSucceeded(accept, released)
WaitingPr -d-> Done: OnPrMerged\nOnPeriodicCheck(PR merged)
WaitingPr -d-> Abandoned: OnPrClosed\nOnPeriodicCheck(PR closed)

owned -d-> Done: OnPrMerged
owned -d-> Abandoned: OnPrClosed

Abandoned --l-> Implementing: OnIssueAssigned\n<delegated again>

Done -d-> [*]
Abandoned -d-> [*]
Dismissed -d-> [*]

note top of NeedsHuman
  Open and not final: an operator retry, a re-assignment or a
  comment sends it back to work with a fresh corrective budget.
end note

@enduml
